- op: discuss  # 13cf
  at: '2026-11-10T23:09:57Z'  # 13cf
  by: agent  # 13cf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 13cf
  clock: 3  # 13cf
  nonce: 13cf  # 13cf
  message: "Fixed in PR #2124 (merged, dd843076c6..7ad2a2de88). Owner-approved 11-10, both parts, auto-pr without --gov.\n\nROOT CAUSE. scripts/generate-schema put REPO_ROOT/src on sys.path, the layout before packages/, so it imported hypergumbo_core only from an installed copy. The hook read its ModuleNotFoundError (exit 1) as \"out of date\", because the hook discarded the output and treated every non-zero exit as stale.\n\nFIX.\n(1) generate-schema now resolves packages/hypergumbo-core/src. All three generators share scripts/generator_check.py: 0 fresh, 1 stale, 2 could not run, with the reason and an activate hint on stderr.\n(2) The hook's check_generated helper prints \"Out of date\" for exit 1, and \"could not run (exit N), so freshness is unknown\" plus the error for anything else; both still block. require_module guards confidence sites (hypergumbo_core) and tracker validate (hypergumbo_tracker), only inside each check's staged-files branch. The plan's hook-wide preflight was narrowed on measurement: after (1), no other check needs the venv, so a hook-wide gate would block commits that pass.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE.\n- The failing case, re-run: the fix commit itself was made from a shell where `python3 -c \"import hypergumbo_core\"` raised ModuleNotFoundError. The hook printed \"Schema (freshness)... ✓\" and the commit succeeded. Before the fix the same shell printed \"Schema is out of date\".\n- On merged dev without the venv: `./scripts/generate-schema --check` gives rc 0, \"OK: docs/schema.json is up-to-date\". A copy outside the checkout run under `python3 -S` gives rc 2, \"ERROR: could not run: ModuleNotFoundError ... Run: source .venv/bin/activate\".\n- tests/test_generator_check.py and tests/test_pre_commit_could_not_run.py: 75 passed together with test_generate_concept_axes and test_schema.\n- Three mutation controls each turned a test red: the stale src/ path, the hook treating every failure as stale, and run() without its crash catch.\n- Branch smart-test run: 6441 passed, 15 xfailed, 0 failed. PR CI is green."  # 13cf
